  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.4\n- BREAKING: IDocumentDetector.Detect removed; replaced by ValueTask<DetectionResult> DetectAsync(CameraFrame, DetectionOptions, CancellationToken)\n- BREAKING: CameraFrame.Data is now byte[]? (null when the platform keeps pixel data on-device, e.g. a live video element)\n- BREAKING: ICameraProvider gains GetFrameDimensionsAsync (intrinsic live-frame dimensions, no byte transfer)\n- Added: CameraPermission.NotSupported and CameraPermission.NotAvailable; RequestPermissionAsync never throws for expected camera failures (missing hardware, busy device, unsupported API, denial)\n\n1.0.0-preview.3\n- Fixed JS Interop Issues and etc..\n\n1.0.0-preview.2\n- Breaking: flattened all namespaces to Circuids.Frame (removed Configuration, Contracts, Results, Events, Export, Extensions sub-namespaces)\n- All public types now in Circuids.Frame root namespace\n\n1.0.0-preview.1\n- Initial preview release\n- Platform-neutral Core: configuration, results, events, contracts, and DI extension\n- Camera access and lifecycle contract (ICameraProvider) with permission request support\n- Document detection contract (IDocumentDetector) with high-level sensitivity and performance knobs\n- Capture pipeline contract (ICapturePipeline) for perspective-corrected capture\n- Image enhancement contract (IImageProcessor)\n- PDF export contract (IPdfExporter) with programmatic byte generation and print dialog modes\n- FrameOptions with sensible defaults for zero-configuration scanning\n- Immutable result records: FrameScanResult, DetectionResult, CornerPoints, ImageDimensions\n- CameraPermission enum: NotDetermined, Granted, Denied\n- AddFrame DI extension (idempotent, order-independent)",
